From 9e3883bb343cab71d03501197268c9d057e1ab20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Geiger <tom@here-be-dragons.ai>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:29:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Kolibri 1 (Aleph Alpha) text model

Kolibri 1 is a 78B-A3.5B MoE: 50 layers, 384 routed experts (top 6) plus
one ungated shared expert, GQA 48/4 with per-head QK RMSNorm, 4:1
sliding-window (513 keys incl. the query) to full attention, RoPE only in
the sliding-window layers, sandwich norms after attention and MoE.

Routing follows the reference vLLM implementation
(Aleph-Alpha/aleph-alpha-inference, kolibri1.py): top-k on
logits + expert_bias, weights sigmoid(logits) of the selected experts,
no renormalisation, fp32 router logits.

The FP8 release loads through the existing block-FP8 path as MXFP8; the
router, embeddings and lm_head stay bf16 as in the checkpoint.
